# L §5.10 (round 14): "A place's price input is named once: on its kind, or on the place itself (its place section or
# its entry), never on both (LOAD-PRICE)"; L §8.4 LOAD-PRICE: "<x> names a price input on its kind <K> and on itself".
# flat's kind homes is priced val and flat states priced val too. (Writer 7: was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.10, U-14.)
=== pr.tally
model pr
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind homes: place PLN min 0 priced val
input val: money PLN
place flat: homes priced val lives 2026-01-01..

ask q: value(flat, 2026-03-01) in PLN law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  val = 5.00 PLN "own"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PRICE flat names a price input on its kind homes and on itself ...
